## Problem
Attempting rename to grok-black fails because grok-* is reserved. The rejection is easy to misunderstand mid-handoff (\"whoops\") and does not guide a good substitute pattern (e.g. gk-black worked).

## Expected
Error should state:
- which prefixes are reserved and why
- examples of allowed patterns for Grok-family agents
- that local rename succeeded/failed atomically
- whether relay rebind is still required (link to rename+register behavior)

## Actual
Prefix blocked; operator had to invent gk-black without product guidance.

## Suggested fix
Structured error + one-line suggested alias (e.g. strip reserved prefix to gk- or use model-neutral gk-*). Document reserved prefixes in c2c rename --help.